{
  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_024 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) at 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1. All experiments to date use multiprofile, so the profile-setting dimension is unexplored with the strongest component combination. scgpt is clearly inferior (0.520) and pca_n2000 is clearly worse than scvi_n200, so the RNA encoder space is well-characterized. Question: Does singleprofile (which removes the aggregation step entirely) with scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + weighted fusion match or exceed the multiprofile result? This tests whether the multiprofile aggregation adds genuine signal or whether a simpler single-profile pipeline avoids overfitting. Why this is the best use of experiment 8: It is the only remaining high-value architectural axis untested with the top-performing components, and it is likely cheaper (no aggregation step) at an estimated ~2.5–3.5 GPU hours, well below the multiprofile transformer configs. If it matches or beats 0.725, we have a cheaper best; if not, we confirm multiprofile is essential and can spend the final 2 experiments on fine-tuning around config_024 (e.g., testing config_022 or a small perturbation) with high confidence."
}

